KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ designated class member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
aggregate_member_initialization paired the initializer-clauses with the
members by position, so `.e = sec(3)' (a designated-initializer node)
became the argument of sec's constructor ("found no match for symbol
'sec'").  The designators now select the members; the others take their
default member initializer or are value-initialized.  This made libstdc++
16.2.0's <chrono> lose __get_leap_second_info.
